

🧩 Blueprint Simulation Engine

Author: C. MATTHEW BLACKWELL — Independent Designer

Purpose: A fully deterministic, encrypted, field‑agnostic simulation kernel

Below is the complete architecture, structured so you can implement it in any language (Rust, Go, TypeScript, C++).

1. Core Kernel Architecture

The kernel is field‑agnostic. It doesn’t know physics, optics, cost, or anything else.It only knows how to:

load fields

run rules

apply patches

validate constraints

arbitrate failures

commit state

sign transitions

Everything else is modular.

2. Field Module Interface

Every field implements the same interface:

Field Module

init(config) -> state

step(state, context) -> state

apply_patch(state, patch) -> state

validate(state, context) -> Violation[]

project(state, view_config) -> Geometry | Metadata

Fields can represent:

optics

structure

thermal

cost

permissions

AI agents

anything you invent later

The kernel never inspects field internals.

3. Rule Module Interface

Rule Module

apply(fields, context) -> PatchSet

Rules generate patches, not direct state changes.

4. Constraint Module Interface

Constraint Module

check(fields, context) -> Violation[]

Violations include:

severity

scope

field_ids

code

metadata

5. Global Arbitration Layer

Global Arbitration

When constraints fail:

Collect violations

Group by severity/scope

Match against policy profile

Generate a ResolutionPlan

Apply actions:

REPAIR_PATCH

CLAMP_INPUT

DEGRADE_MODE

SKIP_RULE

QUARANTINE_SEGMENT

ROLLBACK

This makes the engine self‑healing.

6. Declarative Policy Layer

Policy Profiles

Policies are YAML/JSON files that define:

what to do for each violation pattern

retry limits

mode transitions

allowed mitigations

This externalizes governance.

7. Telemetry Ingestion Layer

Telemetry Pipeline

WebSocket → JSON → normalized → context.telemetry

Validated, rate‑limited, and versioned

Feeds rules and constraints in real time

This connects hardware → simulation.

8. Projection Layer (3D Asset Output)

3D Projection

Each field exports geometry

Kernel assembles scene graph

Exporters produce:

OBJ/MTL

GLTF/GLB

Metadata embedded:

TransitionHash

Signature

Telemetry frame

Policy profile

Mode

Cost (when cost field added)

This connects simulation → assets.

